I have a complete picture. Here is the report on the owner identity feature.

## Overview

The repository is a Spring PetClinic variant. The "owner identity" feature lives across `util/` (pure derivation helpers), `rest/function/owner/` (pipeline steps for `POST /api/owners`), `rest/audit/` (audit events), `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (response DTO assembly), and the `openapi.yml` DTO schema. There is one acceptance test targeting an as-yet-unimplemented "identity-v2" contract.

Important framing: the **current** response shape is FLAT (`memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId`, `locality`, `timezone` at top level, no `apiVersion`). The single acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.java` asserts a **V2** target contract (`apiVersion=2`, those three grouped under a nested `identity` object) that is NOT yet present in `openapi.yml` or `OwnerMapper`. There is no `schemaVersion` field anywhere.

---

## 1. Region code / locality derivation and timezone

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerRegion.java` — the single source of an owner's region. `of(postcode, city)` prefers the postcode range, falls back to the city table:
```java
public static String of(String postcode, String city) {
    String byPostcode = PostcodeRange.regionForPostcode(postcode);
    return byPostcode != null ? byPostcode : CityRegion.locality(city);
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/PostcodeRange.java` — reverse lookup of region from postcode via inclusive ranges NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099. `regionForPostcode(postcode)` returns `null` when absent/non-numeric/out of range; also has `isValidForCity(city, postcode)`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/CityRegion.java` — fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney`→NSW, `Melbourne`→VIC, `Brisbane`→QLD), `UNKNOWN = "UNKNOWN"`. Methods `locality(city)` and `isKnown(region)`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/RegionTimezone.java` — fixed region-to-IANA table:
```java
private static final Map<String, String> TABLE = Map.of(
        "NSW", "Australia/Sydney",
        "VIC", "Australia/Melbourne",
        "QLD", "Australia/Brisbane");
public static String of(String region) {
    return region == null ? null : TABLE.get(region);
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/FiscalYear.java` — FY starts 1 July, named by ending year; `of(date)`, `label(date)` → `FY<YY>`, `elapsed(from,to)`. Used by MemberId.

---

## 2. Identity derivation — householdId, identityKey, memberId

**householdId** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Household.java` (package-private). Derived deterministically from (lastName, postcode):
```java
static String key(String lastName, String postcode) {
    return canonical(lastName) + "|" + orEmpty(postcode);
}
static String id(String lastName, String postcode) {
    return Sha256.hex(key(lastName, postcode)).substring(0, ID_LENGTH); // ID_LENGTH = 12
}
// canonical = trim, collapse internal whitespace, lower-case
```
Assigned by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHousehold.java`: `owner.setHouseholdId(Household.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode()))`. Household size is computed in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java` (existing members with same householdId + 1). Also consumed by `CapOwnerMembershipLevel.java`.

**identityKey** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java`. SHA-256 hex of `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`:
```java
public static String key(String telephone, String email, String lastName) {
    String raw = normalizedTelephone(telephone) + "|" + normalizedEmail(email) + "|" + Soundex.encode(lastName);
    return Sha256.hex(raw);
}
```
Used for duplicate rejection in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` (409 via `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`), for soft-match flagging in `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`, and surfaced in the DTO by `OwnerMapper.identityKey(...)`.

**memberId** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/MemberId.java`. Format `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`; HASH8 = first 8 upper hex of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`; CHK = Luhn over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`:
```java
public static String of(String region, int fiscalYear, String normalizedTelephone, String lastName) {
    String body = region + String.format("%02d", fiscalYear % 100)
            + hash8(orEmpty(normalizedTelephone) + orEmpty(lastName));
    return body + Luhn.checkDigit(body);
}
```
Also `deduplicate(memberId, taken)` (`-<n>` suffix, smallest n≥2), and accessors `region(memberId)` / `fiscalYear(memberId)` used by the mapper for locality/fiscalYear. Assigned by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMemberId.java`, which derives region via `OwnerRegion.of(postcode, city)`, FY via `FiscalYear.of(registrationDate)`, then de-duplicates against existing owners' ids.

Supporting hashing/phonetics: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Sha256.java`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../util/Soundex.java`, `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../util/Luhn.java`.

---

## 3. Owner response shape / DTO

Assembled by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`. Relevant derived mappings (all top-level, flat):
```java
@Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(locality(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "timezone", expression = "java(timezone(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(identityKey(owner))")
@Mapping(target = "ownerSegment", expression = "java(ownerSegment(owner))")
...
default String locality(Owner owner) {
    return owner.getMemberId() != null
            ? MemberId.region(owner.getMemberId())
            : OwnerRegion.of(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());
}
default String timezone(Owner owner) { return RegionTimezone.of(locality(owner)); }
default String identityKey(Owner owner) {
    return OwnerIdentity.key(owner.getTelephone(), owner.getEmail(), owner.getLastName());
}
default OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum ownerSegment(Owner owner) {
    return OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(OwnerSegment.of(owner.getMembershipLevel(), locality(owner)));
}
```
`memberId` and `householdId` come straight off the entity (no explicit mapping override needed). There is currently NO `apiVersion` mapping and NO nested `identity` object. The `OwnerDto` is generated from the schema.

Schema definition: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, the `Owner` schema (lines ~2110-2351). Relevant flat readOnly fields: `locality` (2159), `timezone` (2168), `ownerSegment` (2198, enum PREMIUM_METRO/PREMIUM_REGIONAL/STANDARD_METRO/STANDARD_REGIONAL), `memberId` (2212), `householdId` (2225), `identityKey` (2235), `fiscalYear` (2254). No `apiVersion` / `schemaVersion` / `identity` object present.

Entity storage: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` holds `memberId` (line 73), `householdId` (76), `namesakeCount` (79), `householdSize` (88), `membershipLevel` (94), `possibleDuplicate` (97), `possibleDuplicateOf` (100), with getters/setters. `identityKey`, `locality`, `timezone` are NOT stored — they are derived at mapping time.

Response is sent by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` (201 Created with `OwnerDto`).

---

## 4. Audit event schema

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/audit/OwnerCreatedEvent.java` — record serialized to JSON `{seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, event}`, `event` always `OWNER_CREATED`, `seq` monotonic:
```java
public record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String memberId, Integer membershipLevel,
        String event) {
    private static final String EVENT_TYPE = "OWNER_CREATED";
    public static OwnerCreatedEvent of(long seq, Owner owner) {
        return new OwnerCreatedEvent(seq, owner.getId(), primaryIdentifier(owner),
                owner.getMembershipLevel(), EVENT_TYPE);
    }
    private static String primaryIdentifier(Owner owner) { return owner.getMemberId(); }
}
```
NOTE: there is NO `schemaVersion` field and NO owner-segment field in the audit event currently. The event's identity is `memberId` only.

Emitted by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/audit/OwnerAuditTrail.java` (`AUDIT` logger, human line + JSON, `AtomicLong sequence`) and invoked from the pipeline step `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`. The welcome notification (separate `NOTIFY` sink) is `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../rest/notify/WelcomeNotifier.java`.

---

## 5. Owner segment (derived region)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerSegment.java` — `<TIER>_<AREA>`. TIER = PREMIUM when membershipLevel ≥ 3 else STANDARD; AREA = METRO when region is a `CityRegion.isKnown` region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else REGIONAL:
```java
public static String of(Integer membershipLevel, String region) {
    String tier = membershipLevel != null && membershipLevel >= 3 ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
    String area = CityRegion.isKnown(region) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
    return tier + "_" + area;
}
```
Consumed only in `OwnerMapper.ownerSegment(...)` (keyed off `locality(owner)`). Not present in the audit event.

---

## 6. Versioning in identity logic

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the only explicit identity version marker. Doc comment `identity-v2`; asserts `$.apiVersion == 2` and a nested `$.identity.{memberId,identityKey,householdId}` with those three absent at top level. This is a TARGET contract; the current mapper/openapi still produce the flat V1 shape, so this test would currently fail.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/v2/` — a `v2` API directory exists but only contains `owners.GET.yml` and `pets.GET.yml` (both minimal: `ListOwnersPage` / list handlers). No v2 create/identity logic yet.
- Other "version"/"V1"/"V2" grep hits (`@Version` in `model/*.java` and repositories, `SwaggerConfig`) are JPA optimistic-locking / Swagger config, unrelated to identity.
- No `schemaVersion` anywhere in the codebase.

---

## 7. Tests touching these behaviours

Test source tree is sparse:

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — asserts the identity-v2 response contract (see section 6). This is the only test directly asserting identity fields.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base (`POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`). Contains the pinned ground-truth tables and algorithm replicas the tests derive expectations from: `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `HOLIDAYS`; helpers `region(city)`, `timezone(city)`, `validPostcode(city)`, `knownOwner(city)`, `structuredOwner()`; and identity algorithm mirrors `sha256hex`, `shaHex(s,n)` (upper-cased HASH), `luhn(s)`. These directly mirror the memberId/region/timezone derivations for exact-value assertions.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — test utility that attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` (default) or a named logger; `messages()`, `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(level, ...)`. Enables asserting audit/notify side-effects (the `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON and welcome line) though no test currently invokes it.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDayTest.java` — business-day rolling only; not identity-related (relevant only insofar as registrationDate feeds the memberId fiscal year).

No dedicated unit tests exist for `MemberId`, `OwnerIdentity`, `Household`, `OwnerSegment`, `OwnerRegion`, `RegionTimezone`, or `OwnerCreatedEvent`; their behaviour is exercised only through the acceptance layer.

